      "body": "When `reconnect` is `false` and the socket closes (not closed by us), the handler returns before calling `setLoading(true)`, leaving `loading` in a stale state. On an initial connection failure, `loading` stays `true` forever while `socket` is `undefined`, stranding the view in a permanent loading state with no recovery path.\n\nSuggested fix (model-generated, not tested):\n```suggestion\n        if (closedByUsRef.current || !reconnect) { setLoading(true); return; }\n```",
